      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not really compatible with any of the other variable types -- string_variable requires explicit options, and bool_variable doesn\u0027t pass anything through unless it\u0027s a true-like value.\n\nI originally had called this string_value_variable, but decided that was just confusing. If we could start over, I\u0027d consider renaming what is currently string_variable to something around option/switch/case/map/etc.\n\nAll of my hikey use cases ended up actually being integers, so I almost implemented %d, but figured that that\u0027s really only error checking on top of %s.",
      "parentUuid": "86b4a4ac_fe6f85a1",
      "revId": "b0935db8c3838e90582fdece217bc956ba951f07",
