      "writtenOn": "2020-04-03T05:03:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It mixes the user-defined values with the properties at the same level, so there\u0027s a chance of conflicts (and general confusion)\n\nAnd partially, string variables require a lot more setup -- another module type, or at least a list of structs if I implement a similar shortcut to bool_variables. Versus a list of strings.\n\nIt just feels like it\u0027s mixing two different concepts that have two different usage patterns most of the time -- it\u0027s either an arbitrary value, or one of a list of known values. (There are times where you could mix, like GRALLOC_DEPTH here: https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/device/linaro/hikey/+/1266869/1  but I just don\u0027t see it as much)",
